    "title": {
     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Two friends played a game where each added 1 or 2 and the first to reach 10 won.\n\"There is a trick,\" said Asha."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "estimate",
     "strategy",
     "goal"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Estimation means finding a number close to the actual answer quickly. To estimate 298 plus 402, round to 300 plus 400, which is about 700.\nIn some games we can plan ahead. In the race to 10, if you reach 7, you win because the other player can only go to 8 or 9 and you reach 10.\nThinking backwards from the goal helps find a winning strategy."
    }
   },
